say hello to the first hot hatch from  Kia with a snoot CGT the Korean car  maker wants to take on the pocket  rockets from Volkswagen and Opel our car  tester Carla Simmons wants to see  whether it's got what it takes let's  start on the outside the seed treads in  line between boy racer aggression and  range-topping style with its aggressive  but sweeping lines the little hot hatch  certainly looks the part with its angry  face but flashes of chrome give it a  more upmarket feel the design is the  work of former Volkswagen designer Peter  Schreyer the Kia looks just as good from  behind as it does from the front the  twin rear light clusters dominate the  rear and the twin exhausts if there's  something special under the hood and  there is a 1.6 liter turbocharged petrol  engine time now to hit the road  Corolla we'll be putting the Kia through  its paces on an old race circuit there's  no better place to unleash all of the  GTS 150 kilowatts of power  she says the seeds is a real hoot to  drive there's a lot of power to tap but  she feels the car doesn't really hook up  well coming out of the turns it's like  there's a delay in getting the power to  the front wheels does d5500 k-fed  sugatas medicines bad but the CGT makes  up for that with its sweet handling that  makes it a real blast to drive in the  twisties the sporting flair on the  outside continues on the inside red  stitching and lettering remind you that  this is no run-of-the-mill car there's  no shortage of buttons and shiny inlays  in here the wraparound seats are crafted  from suede and make you feel like you're  in a race car the Kia doesn't skimp on  spec and is fitted with a handy  rear-view camera to aid parking despite  being in the compact class the seeds  trunk offers a truly cavernous 380  litres of storage space it also has a  false floor in which to store valuables  Cola is a big fan of the inlays on the  steering wheel she thinks it looked the  real deal the only problem she says is  that they can be a bit of a headache at  night they reflect the light from all of  the buttons and gizmos here in the cabin  and that can be a bit of a distraction  when you're trying to drive by they  stand out is a blink lista in this large  beagle or daemon special a plane  converter  the last thing you want is to be  distracted because this hot hatch really  packs a punch it accelerates from zero  to 100 kilometers an hour in just seven  point seven seconds  despite that performance it's not going  to break the bank kia says the car can  cover 100 kilometers with a relatively  low 7.4 liters of gas our test car was a  bit more thirsty and consumed 10 litres  but that's still in line with the  competition time for the final word on  the Kia Corolla thinks it's a genuine  alternative to the other hot hatches out  there but she would like to see a bit  more attention to detail in the interior  all in all though she says the Kia has  got it right with a new CGT another  thing that appeals to her is the price  one person attorney outfitting Kia's  place to step pies the top spec GT track  version that we tested is available in  Germany for around twenty seven thousand  euros
 

